================================================================================================
8  THE RADICAND -- "the count of states below" (L9524, restated L9593)
================================================================================================
  radicand = n - l - 1 + q/2(2l+1)
  (n,l)    n-l-1  lower subshells same l   states below same l    equal?
  (2,0)    1      1                        2                      False
  (2,1)    0      0                        0                      True
  (3,0)    2      2                        4                      False
  (3,1)    1      1                        6                      False
  (3,2)    0      0                        0                      True
  (4,0)    3      3                        6                      False
  (4,1)    2      2                        12                     False
  (4,2)    1      1                        10                     False
  (4,3)    0      0                        0                      True
  (5,0)    4      4                        8                      False
  (5,1)    3      3                        18                     False
  (5,2)    2      2                        20                     False
  (5,3)    1      1                        14                     False
  (6,0)    5      5                        10                     False
  (6,1)    4      4                        24                     False
  (6,2)    3      3                        30                     False
  (6,3)    2      2                        28                     False
  (7,0)    6      6                        12                     False
  (7,1)    5      5                        30                     False
  (7,2)    4      4                        40                     False
  (7,3)    3      3                        42                     False
  n-l-1 == number of complete lower subshells of the same l: always TRUE (l+1..n-1).
  n-l-1 == number of STATES below of the same l: FALSE in 18 of 18 cases tested;
  the two differ by the factor 2(2l+1), which is never 1.  The apposition is exact;
  the head of the sentence ("the count of states below") is not.
  L9587/L9593 give the same term a third reading, "the node count" / node theorem:
    radial nodes = n - l - 1, numerically identical to the subshell count, so no clash there.

